------------------------------------------------------------------------
VFS IMPROVEMENTS — identified 2026-05-10
------------------------------------------------------------------------
These are not crash bugs but will make the VFS cleaner and easier to work
with. See BUGS for confirmed crash/correctness bugs to fix first.

[TODO-VFS-01] sys/fs/vfs/file.c:380 — fgetc: remove leftover debug kprintf
  kprintf("[%s:%i]", __FILE__, __LINE__) fires on every character read.
  Delete this line.

[TODO-VFS-02] sys/fs/vfs/file.c:287-292 — sys_fclose: remove duplicate NULL check
  args->FILE == NULL is checked twice in a row. Remove the second check.

[TODO-VFS-03] sys/fs/vfs/file.c — fread should own offset advancement
  Remove the dependency on each filesystem driver advancing fd->offset
  internally. Fix BUG-VFS-04 (uncomment the offset advance), then audit
  each fs driver to ensure it does NOT also advance the offset, so they
  stay in sync.

[TODO-VFS-04] sys/fs/vfs/mount.c — validate before adding to mount list
  Check that device_find() and vfs_findFS() both return non-NULL before
  calling vfs_addMount(). This also resolves BUG-VFS-08 as a side effect:
  the mount list only ever contains fully-initialized entries.

[TODO-VFS-05] sys/fs/vfs/file.c, mount.c — replace sprintf/strcpy with bounds-checked versions
  fileName[1024] and mp->mountPoint are written with unchecked strcpy/sprintf.
  A long path silently overflows into adjacent stack or heap. Switch to
  strlcpy/snprintf throughout the VFS layer.

[TODO-VFS-06] sys/fs/vfs/file.c:335 — kern_fseek: implement SEEK_SET/SEEK_CUR/SEEK_END
  Once BUG-VFS-06 is fixed, kern_fseek and sys_fseek share the same logic.
  Consider merging them into one shared helper to avoid future drift.

[TODO-VFS-07] sys/fs/vfs/ — complete stub implementations
  The following are empty or always-error stubs that block real userland use:
    sys_rename()  — file.c
    sysRmDir()    — file.c (empty body)
    sysUnlink()   — file.c
  At minimum they should return ENOSYS so callers get a clear error.

[TODO-VFS-08] sys/fs/vfs/stat.c — replace hard-coded 0xDEADBEEF/0xBEEFDEAD magic values
  sys_fstat and sys_fstatat return hard-coded fake stat values. These need
  to be wired up to actual inode/fs data so tools like ls(1) show real info.

[TODO-VFS-09] sys/fs/vfs/namei.c, inode.c — remove or complete #ifdef _IGNORE blocks
  Large sections of pathname resolution and inode management are wrapped in
  #ifdef _IGNORE. Either complete the implementation or delete the dead code
  so the actual code path is clear.
